  "note": "Municipal elections, 17 May 1961; contests in Castle, Clifton and Princetown wards. Ballyholme's three councillors were returned unopposed after a withdrawal (Belfast Telegraph, 5 May 1961, p. 6). Dufferin Ward had no contest: its three members are named in the Northern Whig, 5 May 1961, p. 8 (round 2, 7 Nov 2026). F. C. Tughan, a former Mayor, did not seek re-election. Returned unopposed."
